      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Labor unions in the 20th century played a significant role in mobilizing workers and fostering a culture of collective action, thus giving power back to the people. First, they fought for better working conditions and fair wages, pushing for social and economic reforms that laid the groundwork for greater individual agency and democratization in the workplace. Second, unions helped mitigate extreme wealth disparities and social inequality by advocating for progressive taxation and welfare policies. Lastly, they provided a political platform for workers, enabling them to actively participate in and shape political discourse, ultimately influencing the development of a more inclusive and representative democracy in the US.",
